{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144719,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nTable XII shows the source of this pattern. The BO-selected parameters significantly raised ROC-AUC within FF++ C40 (+0.0063) and Celeb-DF v2 (+0.0031) and from FF++ C23 to C40 (+0.0102), but they significantly lowered it in five transfer directions, by 0.041 to 0.104. The Celeb-DF v2 gain was significant in its own family (Holm-adjusted p = 0.021) but not when the families were pooled as recorded before scoring (p = 0.077). The pattern is consistent with the BO objective, source-validation ROC-AUC, fitting each training source more tightly at the expense of transfer. Two limitations apply: the searches used 12, 12, 8, and 8 trials, which limits how fully each search space was explored, and the objective was close to saturation, with best validation ROC-AUC between 0.9977 and 0.9994. The BO-selected configurations also differed from the fixed recipe in several training parameters at once, so the effect cannot be attributed to any single parameter."}},
